Build DRI (for EGL on the software rasterizers) on QNX, which has no DRM

Mesa builds its DRI interface, which is also how EGL reaches the software
rasterizers, only for systems it lists as having DRM/KMS (Linux, the BSDs,
Solaris, Android), or with zink. QNX has no DRM kernel interface, so EGL
was refused ("EGL requires DRI, Haiku, Windows or Android") although
llvmpipe/softpipe need none. On QNX, with a software gallium driver, build
DRI as the GNU Hurd does ("pseudo-drm": dri2.c and the swrast screens,
without libdrm), which gives EGL's surfaceless and wayland platforms on
llvmpipe/softpipe. libdrm, GBM and kms_swrast stay off (system_has_kms_drm
is still false).

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -361,7 +361,9 @@
 ].contains(true)
 
 with_dri = false
-if with_gallium and (system_has_kms_drm or (with_gallium_zink and (freedreno_kmds.contains('kgsl') or host_machine.system() == 'darwin')))
+# QNX has no DRM/KMS, but the DRI interface is also how EGL reaches the
+# software rasterizers (swrast: llvmpipe/softpipe), surfaceless and wayland.
+if with_gallium and (system_has_kms_drm or (with_gallium_zink and (freedreno_kmds.contains('kgsl') or host_machine.system() == 'darwin')) or (host_machine.system() == 'qnx' and with_gallium_swrast))
   _glx = get_option('glx')
   _egl = get_option('egl')
   if _glx == 'dri' or _egl.enabled() or (_glx == 'disabled' and _egl.allowed())
@@ -424,6 +426,10 @@
   with_dri_platform = 'drm'
 elif host_machine.system() == 'gnu' or (freedreno_kmds.contains('kgsl') and with_gallium_zink)
   with_dri_platform = 'pseudo-drm'
+elif host_machine.system() == 'qnx'
+  # As on the Hurd: the DRI interface without a DRM kernel driver (dri2.c
+  # builds without libdrm), for the software rasterizers.
+  with_dri_platform = 'pseudo-drm'
 else
   # FIXME: haiku doesn't use dri, and xlib doesn't use dri, probably should
   # assert here that one of those cases has been met.
